Subject: streams: rewrite files in place for "w" on OpenVMS

On OpenVMS open() with O_TRUNC on an existing file creates a new version
of it, so a file rewritten with fopen(..., "w") or file_put_contents()
gains a version each time, up to the limit of 32767: a board that
rewrites its cache files would fill up with versions (vms-php PORTING_LOG
#40, probe r_versions).  On VMS _php_stream_fopen() opens an existing file
without O_TRUNC and truncates it with ftruncate(0), which keeps one
version and is what POSIX does (the same file, as fileinode() shows on
Linux).  If that fails, or the file does not exist, the open is the usual
one.
---
--- a/main/streams/plain_wrapper.c
+++ b/main/streams/plain_wrapper.c
@@ -1237,6 +1237,21 @@
 	}
 #ifdef PHP_WIN32
 	fd = php_win32_ioutil_open(realpath, open_flags, 0666);
+#elif defined(__VMS)
+	/* On OpenVMS O_TRUNC on an existing file creates a new version of it, so
+	 * a file rewritten with "w" gains one each time, up to 32767.  Truncate
+	 * the existing file in place instead, as POSIX does. */
+	fd = -1;
+	if (open_flags & O_TRUNC) {
+		fd = open(realpath, open_flags & ~(O_TRUNC | O_CREAT | O_EXCL), 0666);
+		if (fd != -1 && ftruncate(fd, 0) != 0) {
+			close(fd);
+			fd = -1;
+		}
+	}
+	if (fd == -1) {
+		fd = open(realpath, open_flags, 0666);
+	}
 #else
 	fd = open(realpath, open_flags, 0666);
 #endif
